cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use History Globe or its data, please cite it as below. Cite the data
  with the release date given as built_at in api/v1/index.json.
title: "History Globe: an atlas of biblical history"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Arnaut
    given-names: Vadym
    email: historyglobe.vadym@gmail.com
url: "https://historyglobe.app"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArVaViT/history-globe"
repository: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/ArVaViT/history-globe"
contact:
  - family-names: Arnaut
    given-names: Vadym
    email: historyglobe.vadym@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-10-25
abstract: >-
  A free 3D atlas of biblical history in 21 languages: 1,231 places named in
  the Bible, with their verses and proposed sites (1,288 place records in
  all), 746 place articles, 200 answered questions, 54 tours, 329 events, 57
  battles and 2,994 people (STEPBible TIPNR), with state borders by year.
  Licences differ by part: the data (places, names, tours, events, people and
  the open API at https://historyglobe.app/api/v1/) is under CC BY 4.0; the
  place articles and the answered questions are under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0; the
  code, the site and its design are all rights reserved (source-available,
  not open source). Third-party data keeps its own licence. See LICENSE.
keywords:
  - Bible
  - historical geography
  - gazetteer
  - ancient Near East
  - digital humanities
  - open data
license-url: "https://github.com/ArVaViT/history-globe/blob/main/LICENSE"
preferred-citation:
  type: website
  title: "History Globe: an atlas of biblical history"
  authors:
    - family-names: Arnaut
      given-names: Vadym
  url: "https://historyglobe.app"
  year: 2026
references:
